title: Lincoln Assassinated
subtitle: A great travesty
on-arrival: moderate_strength -= 2; radical_strength += 2; president = "Johnson"
tags: event
view-if: year = 1865 and month = 4
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/Lincoln.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
max-visits: 1

President Lincoln was assassinated by John Wilkes Booth while watching a play at Ford's Theatre. Government forces are currently on the lookout for the assassin, but now Lincoln's vice president, southern sympathiser Andrew Johnson, is president, much to our dismay.
